// `@clock.format` used to ignore its pattern and hand back the timestamp it was
// given, so this case is the difference between formatting and not. A fixed
// timestamp keeps it independent of the clock; `clock` is a default-allowed
// permission, which is why `allow` is empty.
t ← "2026-07-31T16:31:13.680626617+00:00"
^ @clock.format(t, "%Y-%m-%d")? + " " + @clock.format(t, "%H:%M:%S")?
